WEBVTT

00:01.410 --> 00:03.330
(Supply Room)

00:05.080 --> 00:06.710
Yuki, you there?

00:07.590 --> 00:08.880
Masachika.

00:08.960 --> 00:10.380
You've arrived.

00:11.220 --> 00:12.420
Why did you ask me over?

00:12.670 --> 00:14.090
You sound so cold.

00:14.180 --> 00:17.640
You should be saying,
"Did you wait long? I'm sorry."

00:18.100 --> 00:20.520
Did you wait long? I'm sorry.

00:20.600 --> 00:22.810
Yes, I was waiting for you.

00:23.270 --> 00:24.690
You two are so close.

00:25.770 --> 00:27.400
You're here too, Alya?

00:27.480 --> 00:30.820
I was here the whole time.
I'm sorry for bothering you.

00:31.280 --> 00:32.570
It's okay.

00:33.070 --> 00:34.490
You jerk.

00:36.570 --> 00:37.410
So?

00:37.490 --> 00:39.870
You want me to tidy up the supply room?

00:39.950 --> 00:40.870
Yes.

00:42.410 --> 00:43.290
Here we go.

00:44.080 --> 00:46.420
As expected of you, you're good at this.

00:46.500 --> 00:47.420
Well, yes.

00:47.750 --> 00:48.790
Masachika.

00:48.880 --> 00:50.880
Can you do me a favor?

00:51.880 --> 00:53.050
Board games?

00:56.760 --> 00:57.680
Here.

00:57.760 --> 00:59.100
Thank you.

00:59.680 --> 01:01.100
There are even card games.

01:01.350 --> 01:03.890
We're planning to use them
for the school festival.

01:04.390 --> 01:05.810
The other day,

01:05.890 --> 01:09.520
I played these at the new
student council party the other day.

01:10.860 --> 01:12.400
By the way, who won?

01:13.030 --> 01:16.860
Well, I guess you could say I won.

01:17.030 --> 01:18.200
I thought so.

01:18.780 --> 01:20.910
You two, get to work.

01:20.990 --> 01:22.200
Excuse me.

01:22.450 --> 01:24.080
I'm sorry, Alisa.

01:27.580 --> 01:30.340
Hey, pay attention to me.

01:32.840 --> 01:37.300
Talk to me...

01:37.380 --> 01:38.300
- Hey.
- Talk to me...

01:38.390 --> 01:40.260
- What were you thinking when you said that?
- Talk to me...

01:40.350 --> 01:41.680
Aren't you embarrassed?

01:42.470 --> 01:43.810
He didn't notice at all.

01:43.890 --> 01:45.810
I made it so clear to him.

01:47.230 --> 01:52.860
Talk to me...

01:52.940 --> 01:56.110
Talk to me...

01:56.200 --> 01:58.610
(Student Council Office)
Well done, Masachika.

01:58.950 --> 02:00.660
Thank you. You were a great help.

02:00.740 --> 02:01.740
Not at all.

02:02.580 --> 02:04.790
What? You're done already?

02:05.160 --> 02:08.420
Yes, because Kuze came to help too.

02:09.460 --> 02:11.000
Are you Kuze?

02:11.250 --> 02:13.840
I'm Kenzaki,
the president of the student council.

03:35.500 --> 03:37.550
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

03:45.550 --> 03:49.220
(Episode 2 So-called Childhood Pals?)
I've heard you're very talented.

03:49.310 --> 03:50.680
Thank you very much.

03:51.230 --> 03:52.480
I see.

03:52.560 --> 03:54.900
He does feel like a leader.

03:55.150 --> 03:57.820
No wonder he's known
as the marvelous president.

03:58.360 --> 03:59.900
Well then, I'll be going now.

04:01.780 --> 04:04.110
Wait. You came all the way to help out.

04:04.200 --> 04:06.120
I can't let you go home like this.

04:06.450 --> 04:08.830
If you don't mind,
at least let me treat you to a meal.

04:08.910 --> 04:10.910
No, thank you for your kindness.

04:11.210 --> 04:12.710
Isn't this great?

04:12.960 --> 04:15.750
Even if you go home,
there's no dinner anyway.

04:18.550 --> 04:21.220
Why do you know
so much about Kuze's family?

04:21.550 --> 04:22.880
Because we're childhood pals.

04:24.180 --> 04:25.090
Is that so?

04:25.470 --> 04:28.220
Well, this is perfect.

04:28.310 --> 04:30.310
Suou and Kujou, come with us.

04:30.770 --> 04:31.890
Thank you in advance.

04:32.180 --> 04:33.310
Sure.

04:33.980 --> 04:34.980
Seriously?

04:38.270 --> 04:40.150
Well, I can only afford
a family restaurant.

04:41.780 --> 04:42.820
By the way,

04:42.900 --> 04:45.110
well done for finishing
in such a short time.

04:45.200 --> 04:47.910
I was prepared to do it tomorrow.

04:48.160 --> 04:50.200
Masachika is really amazing.

04:50.580 --> 04:53.080
He can do both the manual work
and paperwork.

04:53.460 --> 04:56.080
He's also good at negotiating.

04:56.500 --> 04:58.000
You flatter me.

04:58.090 --> 05:00.590
It's rare for Suou
to praise someone so highly.

05:01.090 --> 05:02.010
Well, Kuze,

05:02.090 --> 05:03.720
will you join the student council?

05:04.800 --> 05:06.130
I'm sorry.

05:06.220 --> 05:08.430
I don't want to join
the student council anymore.

05:08.510 --> 05:10.100
I had a hard time in middle school.

05:11.890 --> 05:15.390
It's true that the workload
is heavier in high school.

05:15.480 --> 05:17.480
But that's why it's worth trying.

05:17.980 --> 05:19.060
Frankly speaking,

05:19.270 --> 05:21.530
it will even greatly affect your grades.

05:23.110 --> 05:24.400
It's a shame.

05:24.490 --> 05:27.200
I'm not that ambitious or motivated.

05:27.280 --> 05:28.280
Don't say that.

05:28.370 --> 05:29.870
Join the student council with me.

05:29.950 --> 05:31.910
Then we'll run for the president.

05:31.990 --> 05:33.910
Don't ask for more.

05:34.450 --> 05:36.710
Besides, even without me,

05:36.790 --> 05:39.380
you can easily become
the student council president.

05:39.750 --> 05:43.380
But I want to work with you
in the student council.

05:43.460 --> 05:44.720
No, that's too much hassle!

05:46.380 --> 05:48.220
Kuze, just so you know,

05:48.300 --> 05:50.800
if you think Suou will win, you're wrong.

05:51.180 --> 05:53.020
There are other candidates.

05:53.100 --> 05:54.020
More importantly,

05:54.100 --> 05:56.440
Kujou wants to run for it too.

05:57.980 --> 05:59.900
- You too, Alya?
- Yes.

06:00.190 --> 06:03.030
I'll be competing with Suou next year.

06:07.570 --> 06:08.990
Thank you for waiting.

06:11.280 --> 06:12.830
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

06:13.870 --> 06:15.540
Suou and I will go this way.

06:15.790 --> 06:17.710
Please walk Kujou home.

06:17.960 --> 06:18.870
Okay.

06:20.790 --> 06:22.040
Well then, let's go.

06:22.380 --> 06:25.380
You don't have to walk me home.

06:25.800 --> 06:27.720
I can't do that.

06:32.760 --> 06:33.680
Alya.

06:33.760 --> 06:34.680
What?

06:35.180 --> 06:38.350
Are you really going
to run for student council president?

06:38.690 --> 06:40.810
Yes, I told you earlier.

06:46.860 --> 06:48.240
Just drop me off here.

06:48.320 --> 06:49.240
Thank you.

06:49.450 --> 06:50.360
You sure?

06:50.450 --> 06:52.120
- Bye.
- Bye.

07:11.890 --> 07:13.390
(Teach Me How to Love)
Welcome home.

07:13.470 --> 07:15.310
Did you see Alisa home safely?

07:15.760 --> 07:16.970
No. Why are you here?

07:17.060 --> 07:19.100
Because I'm staying here tonight.

07:19.180 --> 07:21.520
- I didn't know.
- I didn't tell you.

07:22.060 --> 07:24.730
Okay, so it's a mysterious handsome man

07:24.820 --> 07:26.020
walking with the heroine?

07:26.110 --> 07:27.530
It has to be a brother.

07:27.610 --> 07:29.400
Judging by this, he should be older.

07:29.650 --> 07:32.110
Usually, you can tell at a glance
that they are siblings.

07:32.200 --> 07:34.620
Why didn't the heroine notice?

07:34.990 --> 07:36.740
No, you have no right to say that.

07:37.540 --> 07:40.080
You insisted on the childhood pals
set-up in school.

07:40.160 --> 07:41.620
You have no right to say that.

07:41.920 --> 07:42.750
What?

07:42.830 --> 07:44.290
That's not a set-up.

07:44.380 --> 07:46.920
Do you really know
what a childhood pal is?

07:47.380 --> 07:49.970
Someone you've been
friends with since childhood?

07:50.050 --> 07:51.010
That's right!

07:51.090 --> 07:54.220
In other words,
siblings are childhood pals too.

07:54.300 --> 07:57.010
Childhood pals, otaku friends,
or real sisters,

07:57.100 --> 07:59.100
they can coexist!

07:59.180 --> 08:00.480
That's a ridiculous logic.

08:01.060 --> 08:03.100
It's not absurd.

08:03.190 --> 08:05.610
It's just a metaphorical explanation.

08:08.780 --> 08:10.320
Wait.

08:11.070 --> 08:14.070
The man who was with
the heroine was her brother.

08:14.160 --> 08:15.570
Of course.

08:16.410 --> 08:17.910
But he kissed the heroine.

08:18.080 --> 08:18.990
Seriously?

08:19.080 --> 08:20.000
Yes.

08:20.870 --> 08:23.580
It's going to be a masterpiece.

08:23.870 --> 08:25.000
No, that's not it.

08:25.580 --> 08:27.000
Logically speaking,

08:27.090 --> 08:28.960
it means
they aren't blood-related siblings?

08:29.880 --> 08:31.090
You idiot!

08:31.420 --> 08:33.800
Real siblings make the story even better!

08:35.180 --> 08:38.810
(Yuki Suou,
Masachika's real younger sister)

08:42.600 --> 08:45.190
Good morning, my brother.

08:45.650 --> 08:47.270
Just now, because of you,

08:47.360 --> 08:48.770
my morning is not good at all.

08:48.860 --> 08:49.730
Hey.

08:49.820 --> 08:53.110
This is a cute little sister's
wake-up pounce on her brother.

08:53.280 --> 08:54.200
You should be happy.

08:54.280 --> 08:56.700
Don't say it like it's a wake-up call.

08:56.780 --> 08:58.200
This is just DV.

08:58.370 --> 09:00.620
A regular Dear Venus?

09:00.700 --> 09:02.620
Come on.

09:02.700 --> 09:04.500
You have a sister complex.

09:04.580 --> 09:06.830
It's DV for domestic violence!

09:08.250 --> 09:10.170
You're hopeless.

09:10.250 --> 09:13.090
Next time, I'll hide under your bed

09:13.170 --> 09:15.590
to grab your legs the minute you get off.

09:15.880 --> 09:18.100
What do you want?

09:18.760 --> 09:20.560
Come on, get off.

09:20.850 --> 09:21.850
Why?

09:22.350 --> 09:23.480
Will you get a boner?

09:23.560 --> 09:24.430
Go to hell.

09:25.060 --> 09:27.400
All right, get up now.

09:27.480 --> 09:30.480
You're going on a date with a cute girl.

09:33.800 --> 09:34.700
(The Movie) (Ever Exciting Space Girl Chi Chi’s
Friendship Adventure)

09:34.700 --> 09:36.030
It's pretty good.

09:36.490 --> 09:37.570
It's so cool.

09:38.280 --> 09:41.120
This special relationship
you only see in movies

09:41.790 --> 09:42.700
is so cool.

09:43.000 --> 09:44.910
Okay, let's watch it again.

09:45.000 --> 09:46.210
- No way!
- Let go!

09:46.290 --> 09:48.420
- We're going shopping now.
- It's calling me.

09:48.500 --> 09:50.420
Hey, don't buy tickets without permission!

09:52.670 --> 09:56.090
I've been wanting
to buy some new summer dresses.

09:56.510 --> 10:00.220
But I'm going to shop
for otaku merchandise later.

10:00.300 --> 10:03.220
It's so expensive! ¥15,000 for a dress?

10:03.470 --> 10:07.390
Women's clothing costs
a lot per piece of fabric.

10:09.480 --> 10:10.810
By the way, Yuki...

10:11.110 --> 10:12.690
What is it, Kuze?

10:13.190 --> 10:17.200
I've been seeing something silver
out of the corner of my eye.

10:17.280 --> 10:18.490
Is it just my imagination?

10:18.570 --> 10:21.200
I don't think it's your imagination,
my brother.

10:21.490 --> 10:22.490
I thought so.

10:22.870 --> 10:25.330
After all, you even let your hair down,

10:25.410 --> 10:27.580
and start behaving so modestly.

10:28.580 --> 10:30.130
Even before you noticed,

10:30.210 --> 10:32.130
I was already aware of her.

10:32.210 --> 10:33.420
No way. Since when?

10:33.670 --> 10:36.010
She showed up
right after we came to this floor.

10:36.090 --> 10:39.010
She's been tailing us for so long?
I'm impressed you noticed.

10:39.890 --> 10:42.720
That's because I have
a super high-performance sensor.

10:42.800 --> 10:44.680
I can sense the gaze of someone I know.

10:44.770 --> 10:45.680
Seriously?

10:45.890 --> 10:47.680
Aren't you ashamed to say that?

10:48.850 --> 10:51.480
- I'm totally embarrassed.
- Don't admit it so seriously.

10:52.310 --> 10:54.610
So, what should we do?

10:54.690 --> 10:56.030
Oh, Alisa?

10:56.780 --> 10:58.610
Hey, Yuki!

11:00.450 --> 11:02.120
Well, if it isn't Alya!

11:02.200 --> 11:03.280
What a coincidence.

11:06.700 --> 11:08.290
What... a coincidence.

11:08.500 --> 11:11.380
Well, actually, I just noticed you two.

11:11.460 --> 11:14.130
But I couldn't find the right time
to talk to you.

11:14.670 --> 11:16.460
- Just? I think not.
- Just? Don't think so.

11:16.960 --> 11:19.720
Alisa, what brings you here today?

11:20.010 --> 11:22.260
Well, I'm here to buy some clothes.

11:22.340 --> 11:23.300
I see.

11:23.390 --> 11:25.010
Have you had lunch?

11:25.260 --> 11:26.890
No, not yet.

11:27.180 --> 11:28.810
Since we've run into each other,

11:28.890 --> 11:30.600
do you want to have lunch together?

11:30.690 --> 11:32.020
- We happen to--
- Wait.

11:32.100 --> 11:35.020
You're not thinking of taking Alya
to that place, are you?

11:35.270 --> 11:37.110
Can't I?

11:37.360 --> 11:40.450
Masachika, you're looking forward
to it too, right?

11:40.530 --> 11:42.200
No, I don't think so.

11:42.280 --> 11:43.280
If Alya is coming too,

11:43.370 --> 11:44.830
it's better to eat elsewhere.

11:44.910 --> 11:47.240
Why? Is there a problem?

11:47.740 --> 11:48.790
Alisa.

11:48.870 --> 11:50.710
Do you dislike spicy food?

11:51.080 --> 11:52.290
Spicy food?

11:52.620 --> 11:54.920
(Instant Curry, Sweet)
No, I don't dislike it.

11:55.460 --> 11:56.880
We're going to a restaurant

11:56.960 --> 11:59.090
that specializes in spicy ramen.

11:59.460 --> 12:02.430
If you don't mind spicy food,
would you like to join us?

12:02.680 --> 12:04.390
Don't just gloss over it.

12:04.970 --> 12:06.680
Alya, I'll be honest with you.

12:06.850 --> 12:08.350
It's not just any spicy ramen.

12:08.430 --> 12:10.020
It's super spicy.

12:10.100 --> 12:10.930
I'll go.

12:11.350 --> 12:13.810
No, you don't have to.

12:13.900 --> 12:16.020
Would I be in the way?

12:16.110 --> 12:17.610
That's not it.

12:18.650 --> 12:21.650
(Hell's Cauldron)

12:22.570 --> 12:23.820
Is this the place?

12:24.360 --> 12:25.200
Yes.

12:25.280 --> 12:27.780
It's called "Hell's Cauldron."

12:27.870 --> 12:29.790
This is definitely a ramen shop, right?

12:29.950 --> 12:31.290
Yes, it's a ramen shop.

12:31.750 --> 12:34.540
But it has "Hell" in the name.

12:34.630 --> 12:36.000
Don't worry.

12:36.080 --> 12:37.880
It's on the menu items too.

12:38.460 --> 12:39.590
I see.

12:40.380 --> 12:41.800
We'd better not go in.

12:41.880 --> 12:43.510
Why not?

12:43.590 --> 12:45.010
I just think it seems unique,

12:45.090 --> 12:46.600
so I was a bit creeped out.

12:47.100 --> 12:48.100
Is that so?

12:49.890 --> 12:50.890
Welcome.

12:50.970 --> 12:52.230
Table for three?

12:52.310 --> 12:53.600
Please have a seat here.

12:53.730 --> 12:55.690
(Hell's Cauldron)
(Blood Pond Hell, Needle Hell, Infinite Hell)

12:56.060 --> 12:58.400
I can't tell what's what.

12:58.690 --> 12:59.610
Exactly.

12:59.860 --> 13:01.110
Blood Pond Hell

13:01.190 --> 13:03.400
is a ramen with a red soup base.

13:03.490 --> 13:05.280
It's also the least spicy.

13:05.780 --> 13:07.200
As for Needle Hell,

13:07.450 --> 13:10.910
it's so spicy that it seems like
there are needles pricking your tongue.

13:12.450 --> 13:14.790
What about Infinite Hell?

13:15.040 --> 13:18.790
That's said to be so spicy
that you'll feel numb after eating it.

13:20.170 --> 13:23.050
I'll have Blood Pond Hell then.

13:23.260 --> 13:27.470
It's best to start with the basics
if you're here for the first time.

13:27.550 --> 13:29.010
That's... true.

13:29.100 --> 13:30.720
The basics are important.

13:31.060 --> 13:33.770
You'll have the Blood Pond Hell?

13:34.270 --> 13:37.730
I'll have the same, then.

13:38.360 --> 13:40.980
Three bowls of Blood Pond for table five.

13:44.780 --> 13:45.820
By the way,

13:45.900 --> 13:49.160
Suou, you're in a boyish style today.

13:49.240 --> 13:50.620
I'm a bit surprised.

13:51.870 --> 13:53.330
It's a holiday, after all.

13:53.580 --> 13:55.290
That's why I'm trying a new style.

13:55.790 --> 13:58.580
I see. Because it's a holiday?

14:00.380 --> 14:01.500
Actually, this morning,

14:01.590 --> 14:04.010
I was lying in bed with Masachika.

14:04.670 --> 14:06.510
Lying in bed together?

14:07.300 --> 14:08.220
Yes.

14:08.430 --> 14:10.180
I told Masachika

14:10.260 --> 14:13.430
that I wanted to wear something different.

14:13.640 --> 14:15.680
That's why he lent me this shirt.

14:16.560 --> 14:17.980
What's going on?

14:18.060 --> 14:20.730
No, she came to my house
and went into my room without asking.

14:20.810 --> 14:23.400
Then she climbed onto my bed.
I'm telling the truth!

14:25.190 --> 14:26.700
You don't seem to believe me.

14:26.990 --> 14:29.910
Sorry to keep you waiting.
Your three bowls of Blood Pond.

14:33.580 --> 14:34.910
It's here.

14:35.290 --> 14:37.080
Let's eat before the noodles get soggy.

14:37.160 --> 14:38.040
Okay.

14:39.290 --> 14:40.790
You're right.

15:03.730 --> 15:05.110
Alya, are you okay?

15:06.360 --> 15:08.490
Yes, it's delicious.

15:13.870 --> 15:15.790
- It's delicious.
- Right?

15:15.870 --> 15:17.200
The spiciness of the togarashi

15:17.290 --> 15:19.290
brings out the umami of the ingredients.

15:19.670 --> 15:21.580
My mouth hurts.

15:23.000 --> 15:25.500
Alya, you don't have to force yourself.

15:25.960 --> 15:28.470
What are you talking about?
Didn't I say it's delicious?

15:28.550 --> 15:30.800
No, you said it hurts.

15:32.470 --> 15:34.760
I can't take it anymore.

15:35.810 --> 15:36.890
Mom...

15:41.400 --> 15:43.190
- Al--
- Alisa, did you enjoy it?

15:44.360 --> 15:46.320
Yes, it was delicious.

15:46.570 --> 15:47.900
I'm glad.

15:48.190 --> 15:50.740
So you like spicy food too, Alisa?

15:51.150 --> 15:52.200
I heard

15:52.450 --> 15:55.490
you can make it spicier
with this "Demon's Tears."

15:55.950 --> 15:57.910
Would you like some, Alisa?

15:58.500 --> 15:59.830
Hey, Yuki!

16:02.290 --> 16:04.630
She's doing it on purpose!

16:05.710 --> 16:06.800
Okay.

16:07.050 --> 16:08.210
I'll have some then.

16:08.300 --> 16:09.170
Wait, Alya.

16:09.260 --> 16:11.430
I really think you shouldn't add it.

16:11.510 --> 16:13.800
Just one drop won't hurt.

16:32.200 --> 16:33.950
Alya, are you okay?

16:36.780 --> 16:38.080
Where's Suou?

16:39.290 --> 16:41.620
She wanted to buy something
so she ran off.

16:42.290 --> 16:43.210
I see.

16:43.750 --> 16:44.790
Are you okay?

16:45.290 --> 16:46.340
What do you mean?

16:46.420 --> 16:47.790
You're still asking me that?

16:50.840 --> 16:52.090
Do you want ice cream?

16:53.430 --> 16:54.380
Yes.

17:07.980 --> 17:09.070
Hey, Alya.

17:09.150 --> 17:10.030
What?

17:10.480 --> 17:13.700
Alya, why do you want to run
for student council president?

17:13.780 --> 17:15.490
Because I want to, of course.

17:17.240 --> 17:19.580
If there's room for improvement,
I have to go for it.

17:19.660 --> 17:20.790
Do I need a reason?

17:24.580 --> 17:26.420
Have you found someone
to team up with you?

17:26.500 --> 17:29.380
No, but it's okay not to have one.

17:29.460 --> 17:31.210
I don't need a vice president.

17:31.300 --> 17:32.710
You don't need one?

17:33.050 --> 17:36.510
You'll need a vice president as long as
they require you to run as a team.

17:37.890 --> 17:40.720
I can just find
a vice president in name only?

17:41.060 --> 17:44.100
I'll get someone to help.

17:44.600 --> 17:45.480
I see.

17:49.360 --> 17:51.530
If you're willing to join me...

17:56.490 --> 17:59.780
Dad, Mom, I'm sorry.

18:00.580 --> 18:01.740
I'm sorry.

18:10.460 --> 18:12.710
Kuze, do you have plans after this?

18:13.380 --> 18:14.800
No, I don't.

18:15.170 --> 18:16.510
What about Suou?

18:17.180 --> 18:20.100
I think we can meet up with her later.

18:20.180 --> 18:21.140
Is that so?

18:21.220 --> 18:23.390
Can you go shopping with me then?

18:23.680 --> 18:25.100
Shopping with you?

18:25.180 --> 18:27.190
You said you're here
to buy clothes, right?

18:27.480 --> 18:28.310
That's right.

18:28.480 --> 18:30.060
How can you say that so openly?

18:30.360 --> 18:32.940
Letting a guy choose clothes with a girl

18:33.030 --> 18:36.650
is something
that only intimate couples do.

18:36.740 --> 18:37.700
Is that so?

18:38.660 --> 18:39.700
I see.

18:40.200 --> 18:43.700
It's probably because she has
no friends to go shopping with.

18:43.790 --> 18:45.910
That's why she doesn't
know the difference.

18:47.460 --> 18:49.080
Right, I'll go with you then.

18:49.670 --> 18:51.170
Why the sudden change of mind?

18:51.250 --> 18:53.130
It's nothing. We're friends after all.

18:53.920 --> 18:56.380
Something doesn't feel right.

18:57.170 --> 18:58.220
Don't mind it.

19:00.840 --> 19:03.310
Why was he so nice to me just now?

19:04.180 --> 19:05.020
Could it be

19:05.100 --> 19:07.680
that he thinks I can't become
the student council president?

19:08.480 --> 19:10.100
How dare he look down on me?

19:13.070 --> 19:14.480
Well, I'll try on some clothes.

19:14.570 --> 19:15.860
Tell me what you think.

19:15.940 --> 19:16.860
Okay.

19:17.150 --> 19:20.950
I'll do my best to make him blush
with my fashion show.

19:23.280 --> 19:24.280
Wait.

19:24.370 --> 19:27.540
If we're only a curtain apart,
won't he hear me changing?

19:28.580 --> 19:30.620
Kuze, can you step outside first?

19:31.170 --> 19:32.210
Okay.

19:50.980 --> 19:52.600
It suits me so well.

19:52.860 --> 19:53.770
Good.

19:56.190 --> 19:57.990
If he doesn't react at all...

20:00.360 --> 20:01.320
Not bad.

20:03.240 --> 20:04.700
If he dares to say that,

20:04.780 --> 20:06.490
I'll beat him up.

20:09.370 --> 20:10.580
What do you think?

20:11.870 --> 20:12.920
It's so pretty.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.790
Yes, it suits you.

20:15.540 --> 20:16.460
What?

20:16.880 --> 20:19.590
This outfit highlights
your innocence and femininity.

20:19.670 --> 20:22.630
It makes you look even cuter.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.510
Really?

20:24.600 --> 20:25.470
Yes.

20:25.550 --> 20:27.140
I'll change into the next outfit.

20:29.640 --> 20:30.600
What's going on?

20:30.680 --> 20:32.730
I feel like I'm being complimented.

20:33.480 --> 20:36.320
I'm so embarrassed.

20:36.400 --> 20:39.530
I can't believe she can say
that with a straight face!

20:39.610 --> 20:41.030
Are they a student couple?

20:41.110 --> 20:42.610
They're so innocent.

20:42.700 --> 20:43.910
He said I'm cute!

20:43.990 --> 20:45.700
He said I'm cute!

20:51.960 --> 20:55.710
Kuze is surprisingly
good at complimenting girls.

20:55.790 --> 20:56.880
I'm impressed.

20:57.670 --> 21:00.210
Surprisingly... good at it?

21:03.970 --> 21:06.600
I remember she's dressed
quite boyishly today.

21:08.060 --> 21:09.720
What do you think?

21:10.680 --> 21:13.810
You look really cool this time.

21:14.060 --> 21:15.900
After all, you're more of a beauty

21:15.980 --> 21:16.980
than a cute type.

21:17.060 --> 21:19.020
This style looks good on you too.

21:21.360 --> 21:22.690
Really? Thank you.

21:23.360 --> 21:24.700
I'll try another one.

21:26.280 --> 21:28.200
This is cute too.

21:29.080 --> 21:31.080
The mature style is good too.

21:31.870 --> 21:32.910
So cute.

21:33.120 --> 21:34.210
Really cute.

21:34.460 --> 21:35.710
Very cute.

21:36.000 --> 21:37.710
(So cute)

21:37.790 --> 21:40.090
(So cute)
I'm so happy!

21:41.670 --> 21:42.880
Next.

21:44.260 --> 21:45.970
Next.

21:49.470 --> 21:51.600
Isn't this a bit too bold?

21:51.970 --> 21:54.690
But I think Kuze will compliment me.

21:58.270 --> 21:59.610
What do you think?

22:07.240 --> 22:09.200
Alisa is so bold.

22:09.580 --> 22:10.490
Yes.

22:17.670 --> 22:20.210
I want to disappear.

22:20.880 --> 22:22.090
What did she say?

22:22.460 --> 22:24.010
She said she wants to disappear.

22:25.670 --> 22:27.340
She's such an innocent baby.

22:27.430 --> 22:28.340
Who are you?

22:37.480 --> 22:40.020
Well, then. See you on Monday, Alya.

22:41.150 --> 22:42.610
I had so much fun today.

22:42.690 --> 22:44.400
Let's go shopping again sometime.

22:44.690 --> 22:46.320
Yes, let's do that.

22:52.410 --> 22:53.660
I can't believe this.

22:53.740 --> 22:55.660
I put on such a short skirt.

22:55.750 --> 22:58.420
I'll definitely be labeled
as an indecent girl.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.300
Why did they get off at the same stop?

23:05.050 --> 23:05.880
What?

23:06.090 --> 23:07.010
What?

23:07.760 --> 23:08.800
What?
